# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c) on a proposal with a yea and a nay (the Unity Fusion Core's, which the
# AIs vote yea on), opened the way the game opens it (council_p2: council(1, 2, 0), after votes_two has given the factions distinct
# votes). The window as it opens (the seats with the AIs' votes, the proposal and the yea and nay totals at the foot of the panel, the
# three vote buttons); the mouse over a seat (the picture under the portrait changes), off every seat and over the player's own (nothing changes); a click on a seat, which asks
# for his vote (yea, nay) and, answered, buys it (the engine's buy_council_vote, which tells the window with set_vote) and the AI's
# message; then the player's own Yea, which decides the vote (make_resolution: the result box, the buttons put away but OK), after which the mouse over a seat changes nothing; and OK,
# which closes the window and carries the proposal out (+500 energy credits to every faction). The state regions are the window's
# fields (proposal, candidate, result, the governor then, the seat the mouse is over, the arrivals), its votes and the votes' counts,
# the rectangles it laid out, each button's visible flag and id, the Council's globals (in session, pending, the per-faction records),
# the governor, the turns each proposal was last put, and (in the faction tables) the energy and the pledges.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
